From 482dcb4b89325acb5ef28dfb41694940c48f3eae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noel Blatter <noel.blatter@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:04:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fast path covers balanced homodyne detectors and sqrt
 parameter links

Feyer's final evaluation uses a similar setup with slightly different
parameters and components. The public fixture was drawn with
uifo(3, random=True), which picks a balanced homodyne readout in half of
the cases, and benchmark.py reads both kinds. Such setups used the dense
JAX path so far: 9.8 s instead of 0.34 s for the fixture with a homodyne
readout (M4, runs/noel/variant_run.py).

- qhd: the selection vector of the noise detector gets its phase factor
  on the host (EntryPlan.selection), and the phase has a derivative in
  case it is a design variable.
- Parameter links with jnp.sqrt (amplitude modulation) are evaluated on
  the parameter row, with the chain rule in the reverse pass. Other
  linking functions still use simulate_jax.
- runs/noel/test_variants.py compares 21 random UIFO setups with
  simulate_jax. variant_fixture.py and variant_run.py make a variant
  fixture with a reference from the unchanged upstream code and run
  benchmark.py on it.

The public fixture is unaffected: all benchmark arrays are bit-identical.
The shipped bytecode of fast.py and simulate.py is regenerated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
